{
  "resume": "=== Devin Rhodie - Resume.pdf ===\nDevin Rhodie \n\n516-402-0127  \u2022  dkr1418@rit.edu  \u2022  www.linkedin.com/in/devin-rhodie-858bb5267 \n\nOBJECTIVE \n\nSoftware Engineering student seeking a full-time co-op/internship in software \ndevelopment or systems design for Spring/Summer 2026.   \n\nEDUCATION  Rochester Institute of Technology, Golisano College of Computing and Information Sciences \n\nBachelor of  Science, Software Engineering Major  \n\u00b7  GPA: 3.0 | Awarded Dean\u2019s List (Spring 2025)| ENGAGE Scholarship (Merit-Based)  \n\u00b7  Relevant Coursework: Software Design for computing systems, Web engineering, \nHuman-centered requirements and design, Software process and project management, \nSoftware testing, Intro to software engineering, Engineering of software subsystems, \nCybersecurity, Database systems, Computer systems concepts \n\n           Anticipated  May 2027 \n\nSKILLS \n\nTechnical Skills:  \nProgramming Languages: Python, Java, C++, C#, JavaScript, HTML, CSS, SQL, API development \nand Integration, object-oriented design  \nOperating Systems: Windows, Linux(Ubuntu), macOS \n\nPROJECT  Musical Instrument Digital Interface (MIDI) App    \nEXPERIENCE  \u00b7  Created a cross device application handling MIDI protocols for real time music playback.  \n\nJan 2025 - Apr 2025 \n\n\u00b7  Designed C++ software to control MIDI playback with Play, Pause, Stop, and Next functions. \n\u00b7  Implemented dual-mode input system supporting both terminal commands and physical \nbuttons \n\u00b7  Integrated LED feedback and event-driven state handling for real-time playback control. \nOct 2024 - Nov 2024 \nCOMIX GUI application \n\u00b7  Built a GUI-based comic book management app with tools for searching, adding, and editing \ncomics. \n\u00b7  Implemented import/export functionality using  CSV/JSON/XML and persistent data storage. \n\u00b7  Collaborated in a team to combine different subsystem designs into a functional application. \n\nEXPERIENCE  RIT SCOOP \n\nRemote \nAug 2025- Dec 2025 \n\nSoftware Engineer Intern \n\u00b7 Contributed to the development and maintenance of SCOOPortal, a web application \nsupporting the RIT SCOOP program for students and faculty. \n\u00b7 Refactored complex React modal components to improve usability, state handling, and error \nmanagement across multiple user roles. \n\u00b7 Led UI debranding efforts, updating styles, labels, and more for new platform requirements. \n\u00b7 Implemented and enhanced confirmation modals to prevent accidental data loss and improve \nuser feedback during form submission workflows. \nUpperLine Code \nSoftware Engineer Intern \n\u00b7  Created a web application using HTML and JavaScript to display local recycling centers.  \n\u00b7  Collaborated with a partner, focusing on frontend development. \n\u00b7  Designed a user-friendly interface and integrated location based search functionality. \n\u00b7  Presented the project to a cohort of peers, explaining the development process and features. \n\nRemote  \n July 2023 - Aug 2023",
